Build succeeded but chunk >500k warning. Three.js bundle 602 KB. Could split vendor chunk to silence? Not necessary, but for tablet load performance it may be nice to route three into a vendor chunk. That doesn't reduce bytes but caching. Warning only. We could set manualChunks to separate three, and maybe chunkSizeWarningLimit. Since load performance matters, one 157KB gzip is acceptable. But a cleaner build without warning would be better. Add vite.config.js with manualChunks. Does project have vite config? No. Add:

import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
export default defineConfig({
  build: { rollupOptions: { output: { manualChunks: { three: ['three'] } } } }
})

This creates three chunk ~500k and app maybe small, still warning for three chunk likely >500k. Could set chunkSizeWarningLimit: 700. That's just warning suppression. Not necessary. But build's dist currently copies fonts. Verify dist/fonts exists.
